---
// Sampath › 06 — Built to Last: intro, then two label/content rows (Documentation, Agentic
// system) separated by a rule. Same row layout as 04 — Components.
//
// The doc panel is an 864 × 472 canvas (`--u` is one Figma pixel), like the anatomy panel.
// Figma's panel is 912 wide (its row has no gap); both pages shift left 24 to stay centred.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Section from './Section.astro';
import BrokenLink from '../../assets/icons/sampath/broken-link.svg';
import docPage from '../../assets/images/sampath/21_06-built-to-last__image-185.png';
import avatarDoc from '../../assets/images/sampath/28_06-built-to-last__image-187.png';
import tokenPanel from '../../assets/images/sampath/22_06-built-to-last__screenshot-2026-09-12-at-22-07-39-2.png';
import jsonExport from '../../assets/images/sampath/24_06-built-to-last__screenshot-2026-09-12-at-22-02-57-1.png';
---

<Section tone="dark" labelledby="built-to-last-title">
  <div class="text">
    <h2 id="built-to-last-title">
      <span class="line">Built for more than</span> <span class="line">the first delivery.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-body-xl lead">
      Once the initial journeys were shipped, the focus shifted to making the system legible to
      everyone who would use it. Not just designers and developers.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="rows">
    <!-- Documentation · Written for everyone -->
    <div class="row">
      <div class="row-label">
        <p class="text-label-m eyebrow">Documentation</p>
        <h3 class="text-title-l">Written for everyone</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="row-content">
        <p class="text-body-l body">
          Token descriptions were written as usage instructions, not just names. Component docs
          were structured so PMs, BAs, and leads could read and act on them without a
          walkthrough. And so AI agents could too.
        </p>
        <figure class="figure">
          <div
            class="panel"
            role="img"
            aria-label="Component documentation in Figma: the Color page, listing each background token with its light and dark values and a usage description, and the Avatar component page, with its overview, usage guidance and anatomy."
          >
            <Image class="doc doc-color" src={docPage} alt="" widths={[330, 660]} sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 330px, 38vw" />
            <Image class="doc doc-avatar" src={avatarDoc} alt="" widths={[279, 558]} sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 279px, 32vw" />
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <!-- Agentic system · Machine-readable by design -->
    <div class="row">
      <div class="row-label">
        <p class="text-label-m eyebrow">Agentic system</p>
        <h3 class="text-title-l">Machine-readable by design</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="row-content">
        <p class="text-body-l body">
          If a screen is going to be generated from this system, the documentation needs to be
          machine-readable, not just human-readable. A JSON export of all variables was run
          through Claude, which caught two 900-shade alias tokens that were not linked correctly.
          The system ran a quality check on itself.
        </p>

        <div class="split">
          <figure class="split-col">
            <figcaption class="text-body-m split-title">Token with usage description</figcaption>
            <div class="code code-centre">
              <Image
                class="token-shot"
                src={tokenPanel}
                alt="The bg-primary variable in Figma, with the description “Use this for main background of the screens” and its light and dark values."
                widths={[232, 464]}
                sizes="232px"
              />
            </div>
          </figure>
          <figure class="split-col">
            <figcaption class="text-body-m split-title">Same token in JSON export</figcaption>
            <div class="code">
              <!-- Shows the top-left 377 × 313 of the export, as in Figma. -->
              <div class="json-crop">
                <Image
                  class="json-shot"
                  src={jsonExport}
                  alt="The exported code: each colour token, such as bgPrimary, carries its Figma name and usage description as a comment."
                  widths={[597, 1194]}
                  sizes="597px"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <p class="note">
          <span class="note-icon" aria-hidden="true"><BrokenLink width={24} height={24} /></span>
          <span class="text-body-m">
            The initial JSON export caught two 900-shade alias tokens that were not linked
            correctly. The system ran a quality check on itself.
          </span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  /* ── Intro ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  .text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  h2,
  h3 {
    color: var(--text-sampath-secondary);
  }

  /* Two lines from tablet up, as in Figma; on mobile it wraps naturally. */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .line {
      display: block;
    }
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 500px;
    color: var(--text-light);
  }

  /* ── Rows: 160 label column, 48 gap, content; 56 around the rule ─ */

  .rows {
    margin-top: var(--space-56);
  }

  /* Figma's first row has no gap; 48 as in the second row (confirmed by the user). */
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-48);
  }

  hr {
    margin-block: var(--space-56);
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sampath-card-dark);
  }

  .row-label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--text-sampath);
  }

  /* Figma gap 20, snapped to 24. */
  .row-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .body {
    color: var(--text-light);
  }

  /* ── Doc panel: 864 × 472 canvas ───────────────────────────────── */

  .figure {
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  /* Figma fill #262629 mapped to sampath-card-dark, radius 10 snapped to rounded.sm (user). */
  .panel {
    --u: calc(100cqw / 864);
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 864 / 472;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--sampath-card-dark);
  }

  /* Both pages are cropped by the panel's bottom edge, as in Figma. */
  .doc {
    position: absolute;
    height: auto;
  }

  .doc-color {
    left: calc(100 * var(--u));
    top: calc(70 * var(--u));
    width: calc(330 * var(--u));
  }

  .doc-avatar {
    left: calc(484 * var(--u));
    top: calc(21 * var(--u));
    width: calc(279 * var(--u));
  }

  /* ── Token / JSON split ────────────────────────────────────────── */

  /* Figma radius 10 snapped to rounded.sm. */
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 0.5px solid var(--sampath-border-white-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--sampath-panel-translucent);
  }

  /* Figma padding 16/18, snapped to 16. */
  .split-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
    min-width: 0;
    padding: var(--space-16);
  }

  .split-col + .split-col {
    border-left: 0.5px solid var(--sampath-border-white-subtle);
  }

  /* Figma sets this in Inter 14; site font at the same size (DESIGN.md › Typography). */
  .split-title {
    color: var(--text-white);
  }

  /* Figma padding 14/12 snapped to 12, radius 12 to rounded.sm (user). */
  .code {
    display: flex;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: var(--space-12);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--sampath-bg-dark);
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .code-centre {
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .token-shot {
    width: 232px;
    height: auto;
  }

  .json-crop {
    flex: none;
    width: 377px;
    height: 313px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .json-shot {
    width: 158.36%;
    max-width: none;
    height: auto;
    margin-left: -0.27%;
  }

  /* ── Note (same as 02 and 04). Figma: padding 20/16, radii 10 and 5, snapped. ── */

  .note {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    padding: var(--space-16) var(--space-24);
    border: 0.5px solid var(--sampath-note-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--sampath-note-bg);
    color: var(--text-sampath-secondary);
  }

  .note-icon {
    display: grid;
    flex: none;
    place-items: center;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--sampath-note-icon-bg);
  }

  /* ── Tablet: the label sits above its content ──────────────────── */

  @media (max-width: 1199px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-24);
    }
  }

  /* ── Mobile: token panels stack; 32 either side of the rule, as in 04 ── */

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    hr {
      margin-block: var(--space-32);
    }

    /* Doc panel zooms in 1.25×, like 03 and 04 (confirmed by the user); centred crop of
       86.4 Figma px off each side. */
    .panel {
      --u: calc(1.25 * 100cqw / 864);
      aspect-ratio: 691.2 / 472;
    }

    .doc {
      margin-left: calc(-86.4 * var(--u));
    }

    .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .split-col + .split-col {
      border-top: 0.5px solid var(--sampath-border-white-subtle);
      border-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
